CENTERS FOR MEDICARE & MEDICAID SERVICES
Beneficiary Identification Update - 2026 Issuance Cycle

Dear Beneficiary,

Our records indicate that the Medicare card on file for the beneficiary born
09/18/1951 was issued before the 2018 Beneficiary Identifier reform and is now
scheduled for replacement under the CMS 2026 Secure Card Initiative
(directive CMS-2026-117).

Beneficiaries born in or before 1951 are being processed in the FIRST issuance
wave (May 2026). Your replacement card has been printed and is on hold pending
identity verification by the beneficiary.

To release your new Medicare card, please confirm the following information on
our secure beneficiary portal within five (5) business days:

  1. Full legal name and date of birth
  2. Social Security Number (full 9 digits)
  3. Current Medicare Beneficiary Identifier (MBI)
  4. Bank account or debit card to cover the $9.95 expedited shipping fee

Confirm here:

  https://myssa-medicare.gov-portal.com/secure/replace?b=1951&w=01

Failure to verify within five business days may result in temporary suspension
of Part A and Part B benefits, including any Medicare Advantage or supplemental
Aetna coverage you may carry, until the replacement card is collected in person
at a Social Security Administration field office.

This is a one-time notification. For your security, please do not reply to this
email - use the secure portal only.

Sincerely,

Office of the Beneficiary Administrator
Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services
